aw.githubusercontent.com/webagent-cloud/webagent/21969388bbb70a0ebf44aee0a8a913ccc54d294e/webagent/llm_service.py"},{"method":"license_header","retrieved_at":"2026-10-20T04:44:29Z","role":"primary","sha256":"8149145076020a5c142fb8fd03463a2da2cadce98aa703ac6746f40cb5ee8f6b","supports":["licenses.code"],"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webagent-cloud/webagent/HEAD/LICENSE"}],"id":"github:webagent-cloud/webagent","identifiers":{},"kind":"agent","last_verified_at":"2026-10-20T07:41:55Z","licenses":{"code":{"basis":"repository LICENSE header; not a weights/data license","declared":"MIT","retrieved_at":"2026-10-20T04:44:29Z","url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webagent-cloud/webagent/HEAD/LICENSE"},"data":null,"document":null,"weights":null},"links":[{"rel":"primary","url":"https://github.com/webagent-cloud/webagent"}],"name":"Webagent (webagent.cloud)","notes":"Open-source code of the webagent.cloud hosted service, published by webagent-cloud. A FastAPI server (server.py, webagent/api.py) with a bundled React UI accepts a prompt and runs it with the engine set by ENGINE_PROVIDER: Browser Use by default, or Notte, whose agent is fixed to gemini-2.5-flash with at most 30 steps. The browser comes from BROWSER_PROVIDER: a local Playwright Chromium over CDP, Browserbase or Steel; at the reviewed commit the Steel provider's create_session takes a context argument that the caller does not pass. Models are reached through Browser Use's chat clients for OpenAI, DeepSeek, Anthropic, Google and Groq; other provider values fall back to the OpenAI client. After a run, workflow_builder_service.py asks an LLM to extract parameters from the prompt and template the recorded actions with their element XPaths; workflow_replay_service.py replays those steps with Playwright (navigation, search, XPath clicks and typing, scrolling, key presses, uploads, dropdowns) without a model and, when an action fails, hands that step to the AI engine for up to three attempts. Tasks, runs and results are kept in a local SQLite database; results can be text or JSON validated against a supplied JSON Schema, and a webhook can be called on completion. The README's n8n, Zapier and Make integrations and Stagehand engine are not in the tree. Root LICENSE is MIT; not a fork, not archived; no release. Code was read, not run.","published_at":null,"relations":[{"evidence_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webagent-cloud/webagent/21969388bbb70a0ebf44aee0a8a913ccc54d294e/webagent/engine_providers/browseruse_service.py","target_id":"github:browser-use/browser-use","type":"uses"},{"evidence_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/webagent-cloud/webagent/21969388bbb70a0ebf44aee0a8a913ccc54d294e/webagent/engine_providers/notte_service.py","target_id":"github:nottelabs/notte","type":"uses"}],"review_status":"curated","scope":"core","summary":"Self-hostable browser-agent server that runs Browser Use or Notte agents, turns a run's recorded actions into a parameterized workflow, and replays it with Playwright, falling back to the agent when a step fails.","topics":["automation","workflow","web-navigation"],"updated_at":null,"url":"https://github.com/webagent-cloud/webagent"}
